# Writes target\t05\s02-expected.md (drafter-owned): each step's expected outputs, each with the doc line it comes from, quoted from the file with the
# line number that Select-String finds NOW. A quote whose text is not found stops the run with exit 1, so the file never cites a line it did not read.
# RFC 2119 keywords; the capitals are load-bearing. Run with pwsh -NoProfile -File.
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
Set-StrictMode -Version Latest
$repo = [IO.Path]::GetFullPath((Join-Path $PSScriptRoot '..\..'))
$sb = [System.Text.StringBuilder]::new()
$script:missing = 0
function L([string]$Text = '') { [void]$sb.AppendLine($Text) }
# A cited line: `file:line: "the line, trimmed"`, from the first line of the file holding the literal $Find.
function Cite([string]$File, [string]$Find) {
  $path = Join-Path $repo $File
  $hit = Select-String -LiteralPath $path -Pattern $Find -SimpleMatch | Select-Object -First 1
  if ($null -eq $hit) { $script:missing++; L "  - NOT FOUND: $File holds no line with: $Find"; return }
  $t = $hit.Line.Trim()
  if ($t.Length -gt 190) { $t = $t.Substring(0, 190) + '...' }
  L ("  - $File`:$($hit.LineNumber): ``" + $t.Replace('`', "'") + '``')
}
function E([string]$Text) { L "- $Text" }

L '# E0.12-T05-S02: the expected values of the windows/amd64 live check, written before any dry run'
L ''
L 'RFC 2119 keywords; the capitals are load-bearing. Drafter-owned, in `target\t05`. **Every expected value is followed by the doc line it comes from**, quoted from the file with the line number a `Select-String` found when this file was written (`s02-make-expected.ps1` writes it and stops when a quote is not found). A value no doc states is marked **drafter''s reading**, with the reason.'
L ''
L '## How a step is run, and what its exit code means'
L ''
L '- **Each step is `target\t05\s02-step-<nnn>.ps1`, run as** `pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts\live\wrap.ps1 -Out target\runs\runner -Name <nnn>-<what> -Script target\t05\s02-step-<nnn>.ps1`. A used name is refused, so a rerun takes the next number. Nothing is passed as a parameter: the knobs are `S02_*` environment variables that a live run MUST NOT set (the loops'' bounds: `S02_POLL_SECONDS` 60, `S02_MAX_SECONDS` 5400, `S02_IDLE_SECONDS` 720, `S02_STOP_SECONDS` 2100; the lease''s TTL `S02_TTL` 4h; `S02_SYSTEM_WINGET=0` skips the transient SYSTEM probe of 315i).'
L '- **Exit codes:** 0 PASS; 1 a FINDING (each printed as a `FINDING:` line; a failure is a finding and is never retried past); 2 the lease ended `unsatisfiable`, `expired` or `released` (311); 3 a loop''s bound was reached (311 at 90 minutes, 341 at 35); 5 STOP, a precondition failed before anything ran (a printed `STOP:` line; also any `AGENTSPACE_*` variable set in a live run); 6 windows/amd64''s hours reached 4.5 (every loop, from the observer''s `hours.json`).'
L '- **Programs:** the installed `agentspace.exe` and `agentspace-operator.exe` by `%USERPROFILE%\.agentspace\bin\`, `ssh`, `scp` and `aws` from the PATH, and `C:\Projects\localswim\localswim.exe` by its full path. No script lists, reads, copies or hashes an installed program, and none names `up`, `sync` (except the optional 316), `bootstrap`, `provision`, `grow`, `deploy` or an arm64 host.'
L '- **Printing:** every line goes through `ConvertTo-LiveMasked` after a replacement of the EC2 computer name (`EC2AMAZ-XXXXXXX`), which `scripts\live\mask.ps1` does NOT cover (shown by running it on `EC2AMAZ-K3F9Q2L\agent`: unchanged). A lease ID or alias is only ever in `target\t05\s02-state\` and prints as `<lease>` or `<alias>`. Times print `h:mmam` in the laptop''s zone, read from the system at each step''s start.'
L ''

